Public SSH Keys in Bicep
Your Bicep Template (main.bicep)

----------------------------------------file below
@secure()
param sshPublicKey string

param vmName string
param adminUsername string

var location = resourceGroup().location

resource vm 'Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines@2023-03-01' = {
  name: vmName
  location: location
  properties: {
    osProfile: {
      computerName: vmName
      adminUsername: adminUsername
      linuxConfiguration: {
        disablePasswordAuthentication: true
        ssh: {
          publicKeys: [
            {
              path: '/home/${adminUsername}/.ssh/authorized_keys'
              keyData: sshPublicKey  // Your public key goes here
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
    // ... other VM properties
  }
}
----------------------------------------end


Your Bicep Parameter File (main.bicepparam)

Bicep has its own parameter file format (.bicepparam):


-----------------------------------file below
using './main.bicep'

param vmName = 'myLinuxVM'
param adminUsername = 'azureuser'
param sshPublicKey = 'ssh-rsa AAAAB3NzaC1yc2EAAAADAQABAAABAQC7laRyN... user@machine'
-----------------------------end

This is fine because it's a public key!
Deployment Command

----------------------Using CLI
az deployment group create \
  --resource-group myRG \
  --template-file main.bicep \
  --parameters main.bicepparam
